{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-120856" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate, in degrees, rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions to the equation $9\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-8$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-120856" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-8 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-\\frac{8}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{8}{9})=-62.733\\,955{…}^{∘}≈-{62.73}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-{62.73}^{∘}$ lies inside the range, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-{62.73}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={62.73}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={62.73}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/assets/62808ce876d31757e1b46863b014bbf83209c414099ade0f93b91303c6702d1f.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{62.73}^{∘} \\\\  & ={242.73}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we simply subtract ${360}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=X-{360}^{∘}={242.73}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{117.27}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions (rounded to the nearest integer) are $x=-{117}^{∘},-{63}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-120856" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f636e6e50d9edf14bcdf244b29a4f24ccf7441795f069473544e9cd7831f4138"} {"question" "q-120856" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-120856" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-{104}^{∘},-{76}^{∘}"] ["math" "x=-{107}^{∘},-{73}^{∘}"] ["math" "x=-{111}^{∘},-{69}^{∘}"] ["math" "x=-{117}^{∘},-{63}^{∘}"] ["math" "x=-{121}^{∘},-{59}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-120856" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-{117}^{∘},-{63}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-274619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact solution to the equation  $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$ Give your answer in radians.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-274619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5 & =0 \\\\ 5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-5 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nAs this is a quadrantal angle, to find the remaining solutions, we use our knowledge of the sine function. We know that the sine function has its minimum values at:\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \n$$\n\nSince the domain $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi $ is one period, and we have already found one minimum value in this period, we conclude that $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is the only solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-274619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f636e6e50d9edf14bcdf244b29a4f24ccf7441795f069473544e9cd7831f4138"} {"question" "q-274619" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-274619" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{\\pi}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-332213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions to the equation  $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0.85,$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$   are\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$, $\\,x≈$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-332213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0.85)=58.211\\,669…≈{58.2117}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSince ${58.2117}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={58.2117}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={58.2117}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={58.2117}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/assets/ec4366c4e46cc9c1df5fb31aa2ca04f337fd3c6d0bce034405ca2b48874aa32a.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{58.2117}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈{121.7883}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx≈{58.2}^{∘},\\,x≈{121.8}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-332213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f636e6e50d9edf14bcdf244b29a4f24ccf7441795f069473544e9cd7831f4138"} {"question" "q-332213" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-332213" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "58.2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-332213" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-332213" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "121.8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-332380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{3}{5},$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$  are\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x≈$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-332380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{3}{5})=0.643\\,501…≈0.6435\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $0.6435$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=0.6435.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.6435.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.6435.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/assets/962545fd6fa64e121a99eb8bf684484e4b457dbd4defedd7c07ae88fd47cac6e.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -0.6435 \\\\  & ≈2.4981.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx≈0.6,\\,x≈2.5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-332380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f636e6e50d9edf14bcdf244b29a4f24ccf7441795f069473544e9cd7831f4138"} {"question" "q-332380" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-332380" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-332380" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-332380" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2.5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-336507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact solution to the equation  $4\\sqrt{3}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\sqrt{3}=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Give your answer in radians.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-336507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{3}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 4\\sqrt{3}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-4\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ does not lie inside the required domain $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ we add one full period of $2\\pi $ to find an equivalent angle in the domain:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2\\pi =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\nThus, our first solution in the required domain is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nAs this is a quadrantal angle, to find the remaining solutions, we use our knowledge of the sine function. We know that the sine function has its minimum values at:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \n$$\n\nSince the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is one period, and we have already found one minimum value in this period, we conclude that $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is the only solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-336507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f636e6e50d9edf14bcdf244b29a4f24ccf7441795f069473544e9cd7831f4138"} {"question" "q-336507" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"} {"question" "q-336507" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992768/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc7250420e33b5ca47ee18a3ebda68752f3fda039381faf5bf04eec70db1b4f"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1045 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
